      "message": "feat(kernel): read a Solidcraft design's cached final body\n\ncamcraft_kernel::solidcraft::import_solidcraft reads a Solidcraft .sc\ndesign (a ZIP container) and returns the final body its model cache\nholds, as the same checked solidcore StepSolid the STEP reader hands\nout. Only a cache that is provably this document's is read: container\nsolidcraft-container/1, document solidcraft/<n> in mm, cache format 8\nor 10 from solidcraft-truck-adapter/4 on solidcore, and SHA-256 digests\nthat match document.json and cache/bodies.bin. The final state is\nSolidcraft's own rule (last feature not skipped); its one body's slice\nis decoded by solidcore-record. Every other case is refused by name:\nnot a ZIP, ZIP64, multi-disk, encrypted, duplicate names, over 10,000\nentries or a size cap, CRC-32 mismatch, no cache, unknown versions, a\nstale cache, a payload digest mismatch, bad slices, several bodies, a\nplaced copy, a mesh body, a bad magic.\n\nThe ZIP reader (APPNOTE.TXT) and SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) are written here;\nflate2 (already in Cargo.lock) inflates. build_record is split out of\nthe STEP reader so both share its checks. The maintainer's sample is\nthe fixture; refusals are pinned on corrupted copies built in the\ntests, plus a seeded mutation run under a time bound.\n\nApp wiring (open dialog, drop, MCP) is not in this commit.\n\nRefs #1456\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
