      "message": "fix(kernel): refuse far-off .sc body coordinates; fuzz the body decoder\n\nThe Solidcraft reader now checks every vertex of the decoded final body\nagainst its own coordinate limit, MAX_COORD_MM = 1e6 mm: a non-finite or\nfar-off coordinate is refused by name before the kernel builds anything.\nThe decoder's own bound (1e12) let bodies kilometres away through.\n\nNew solidcraft_hostile tests splice edited or damaged bodies into the\nsample with true digests and CRC-32s, so every case reaches the body\ndecoder: far-off, NaN, infinite and 1e13 coordinates are refused by name;\n24 byte-damaged bodies never panic or hang (120 s bound) and every\nrefusal names the final body; a deflate entry inflating past its\ndeclared size is cut off.\n\nFixes #1467\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
